diff --git a/doc/changelog.rst b/doc/changelog.rst
index a055dde..d4aec3f 100644
--- a/doc/changelog.rst
+++ b/doc/changelog.rst
@@ -24,6 +24,16 @@ General
 - Flex bending and stretching now include the motion and reaction forces of articulated vertex attachments. The discrete
   integrator supports these attachments with the CG solver; fixed and independent XYZ-slide attachments retain their
   optimized assembly. Elastic flexes attached to mocap bodies produce a compiler error.
+- The CG and Newton linesearch now brackets at the constraint zone boundary nearest the bracket midpoint (e.g. where a
+  contact crosses the elliptic cone boundary), and skips Newton candidates that fall outside the bracket. With elliptic
+  cones and a large :ref:`impratio<option-impratio>`, the linesearch could exhaust
+  :ref:`ls_iterations<option-ls_iterations>` without improvement, ending the solve at a non-minimizer (:issue:`3628`).
+- The linesearch gradient tolerance is now floored at the rounding noise of the linesearch derivative. With
+  :ref:`tolerance<option-tolerance>` set to 0, or in single precision, the linesearch no longer exhausts
+  :ref:`ls_iterations<option-ls_iterations>` chasing noise.
+- Added the warning ``mjWARN_LINESEARCH``, raised when a CG or Newton linesearch uses all
+  :ref:`ls_iterations<option-ls_iterations>`. A linesearch that runs out of evaluations without improvement, which ends
+  the solve, is now reported as a solver iteration with zero improvement in :ref:`mjSolverStat`.
 
 Version 3.14.0 (September 22, 2026)
 -----------------------------------
